
I13TEST - the disk BIOS a DOS box sees
  BIOS drive: 80
  AH=08h - the geometry:
    65 x 16 x 63
  AH=02h - the first sector, by CHS:
    OK   read, and it ends AA55
  AH=41h/42h - the extensions:
    OK   present, and they do extended access
    OK   LBA 0 and CHS 0/0/1 are the same sector
  and a CHS triple that does not exist:
    OK   sector 0 refused
    OK   head 254 refused
  and does it agree with the filesystem?
    OK   a file DOS just closed is on the medium
    OK   a raw write went through the cache, not round it
I13TEST done
